d way to apply the exception. It\n./docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-492-runs the action and accepts a failure only on proof, in this order:\n./docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-493-\n./docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-494-1. the thrown `Error` is an `UnsupportedFeatureError`;\n./docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-495-2. an `UnsupportedFeatureError` appears in its cause chain, which also covers\n./docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:496:   `ServiceConfigurationError` and `ExceptionInInitializerError` wrapping;\n./docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-497-3. a throwable carrying an `UnsupportedFeatureError` was printed to `System.err`\n./docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-498-   while the action ran, which is the only surviving evidence when a library\n./docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-499-   discards the cause.\n./docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-500-\n./docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-501-Printed throwables are inspected as objects, never matched as text, so unrelated\n./docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-502-output naming the error cannot buy tolerance. An `AssertionError` or\n./docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-503-`VirtualMachineError` is always re-thrown, so a genuine assertion failure after a\n./docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-504-tolerated one is never masked. Anything else is re-thrown unchanged. On the JVM the action runs and asserts\n--\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-13-\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-14-## Workflow\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-15-\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-16-1. Reproduce the failure:\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-17-   - Run `./gradlew test -Pcoordinates=<coordinates>` from repository root.\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-18-2. Classify the failure:\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-19-   - If the failure is a `Missing*RegistrationError` or GraalVM reports matching metadata that is inactive because its condition was not satisfied, continue with metadata repair.\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-20-3. Capture the missing metadata from the error message:\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md:21:   - Locate any `Missing*RegistrationError` (e.g. `MissingReflectionRegistrationError`, `MissingResourceRegistrationError`, or any other variant).\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-22-   - Copy the suggested JSON entry for the missing type into the corresponding section of the reachability-metadata.\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-23-4. Choose the target file and insert the entry:\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-24-   - Write to `metadata/<library-specific-metadata-directory>/reachability-metadata.json`.\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-25-   - Keep valid JSON and avoid duplicating an existing equivalent entry. If the type already exists but a method or field is missing, add only that method or field.\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-26-5. Add the missing `condition` field:\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-27-   - Infer it from the error stack trace.\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-28-   - Set the `condition` field to `{ \"typeReached\": \"<class>\" }`, where `<class>` is the first class on the stack trace whose package shares the leading namespace with the tested library's package.\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-29-   - Package overlap can be partial, full package equality is not required.\n--\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-38-\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-39-Use this reference when deriving the missing entry and condition.\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-40-\n./skills/fix-missing-reachability-metadata/SKILL.md-41-### Missing Registration Entr